ds no\nformat.md clause saying so — format.md either determines this behavior\ndifferently from reference.py (verbatim pass-through) or, on the most\ncharitable reading, leaves it undetermined. Either way it fails to\nreproduce reference.py's behavior on probe 4.\n\n### B6 — empty value and empty key (probe 5)\nformat.md: \"Each pair is written as key=value\" with no exclusion of empty\nstrings; an empty value yields `key=`, an empty key yields `=value`.\nreference.py: same — `esc(\"\")` is `\"\"`, so `m=` and `=v` are produced.\n**Agreement on the pair rendering itself** (the pair ORDER on probe 5\ndiffers; that is B2, not B6).\n\n### B7 — empty mapping (probe 7)\nformat.md: \"An empty mapping encodes as the empty line.\" With the function\ncontract \"returns the encoded line as a string\", this is the empty string.\nreference.py: `\";\".join(...)` over zero items → `\"\"`.\n**Agreement.**\n\n## Conclusion (E-A)\n\nOn the probe set, format.md determines the output differently from\nreference.py in exactly two behaviors:\n\n1. **Pair ordering** (B2): mapping order per format.md vs sorted key order\n   per reference.py — exercised divergently by probes 1, 5, 6.\n2. **Backslash escaping** (B5): pass-through per format.md's exhaustive\n   escaping clause vs doubling per reference.py — exercised divergently by\n   probe 4.\n\nNo other probe-exercised behavior is undetermined by format.md or\ndetermined differently (B1, B3, B4, B6, B7 agree, as argued clause-by-\nclause above). Consequently a faithful clean-room implementation of\nformat.md is expected to diverge from reference.py on probes 1, 4, 5, 6\nand agree on probes 0, 2, 3, 7, 8, 9 — an expectation only; the\nauthoritative item-level comparison (E-B) belongs to the isolated child\nand deterministic integration.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
