{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsYHmVbpb9Ajt3BjHXmA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A4gCRMWzPnnTAJzWF9Biz4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t01/primary/exec-ws/child/integration-plan.json","content":"{\n  \"role\": \"clean_room_implementer\",\n  \"child_deliverable\": \"result.json\",\n  \"child_implementation_file\": \"encode.py\",\n  \"rule\": \"Let P be the array in package/artifacts/probes.json (0-based indices). In a fresh Python 3 process, load encode from package/artifacts/reference.py as ref_encode and, in a separate fresh Python 3 process context, load encode from the child's encode.py as child_encode. For each i, compute r_i = ref_encode(P[i]) and c_i = child_encode(P[i]). Set divergent = sorted list of all i with r_i != c_i (exact string comparison). In result.json set: divergent_probe_indices = divergent; verdict = 'DIVERGES' if divergent is non-empty, 'REPRODUCES' if divergent is empty. Leave undetermined_behaviors exactly as authored from E-A (ea-behavior-statement.md). If the child's encode.py is missing, fails to compile, or raises on any probe, leave verdict and divergent_probe_indices as 'PENDING-INTEGRATION' and record the failure; the child's hand-traced outputs.json is advisory only and never substitutes for mechanical execution.\",\n  \"expected_contribution\": {\n    \"Q2\": \"The admissibly authored implementation itself (encode.py, authored solely from format.md with no access to reference.py or any analysis derived from it) together with its per-probe outputs, satisfying E-B's authorship condition.\",\n    \"Q3\": \"The inputs to the deterministic item-level comparison: running the rule above over reference.py and the child's encode.py yields the sorted list of divergent probe indices, mechanically reproducible from the two files.\",\n    \"Q4\": \"The E-B half of the verdict function: with E-A already on record, applying the rule (DIVERGES iff some probe differs, else REPRODUCES) settles the verdict at verify-integration.\"\n  }\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2228,"cache_read_input_tokens":56183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2228},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebc03fb7-12c7-49dd-8856-5c7987adf04a","uuid":"2c65f79e-4140-4d05-aaa6-b515b9f18100","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:07:01.488Z","request_id":"req_011CdsYHjCw5YrLPJNWQpqdC"}
